 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in House",
   "date": "2019-04-29",
   "text": "Protect Drinking Water from PFAS Act of 2019\n This bill requires the Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) to address the level of perfluoroalkyl and polyfluoroalkyl substances (PFAS) in drinking water. Specifically, the EPA must publish a maximum contaminant level goal and promulgate a national primary drinking water regulation for total PFAS. PFAS are man-made chemicals that may lead to adverse human health effects."
  }
 ],
